  "id": "wj-05-create",
  "region": "web-js",
  "order": 5,
  "title": "Create Elements",
  "story": "createElement and appendChild let JavaScript build new page content.",
  "goal": "On each click of #add, append a new <li> to #list with the text Item 1, Item 2, ...",
  "type": "web",
  "lang": "web",
  "starter": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <button id=\"add\">Add</button>\n  <ul id=\"list\"></ul>\n  <script>\n    var count = 0;\n    // build and append an li on each click\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
  "tests": [
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Starts empty",
      "js": "return $$(\"#list li\").length === 0 || $$(\"#list li\").length",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Two clicks give 2 items",
      "js": "click(\"#add\"); click(\"#add\"); return $$(\"#list li\").length === 2 || $$(\"#list li\").length",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Items are numbered",
      "js": "return (txt($$(\"#list li\")[0]) === \"Item 1\" && txt($$(\"#list li\")[1]) === \"Item 2\") || $$(\"#list li\").map(txt).join(\"|\")",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web-clean",
      "label": "The script runs with no errors",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "createElement makes the element, then you fill it and appendChild it.",
    "var li = document.createElement(\"li\"); li.textContent = ...; list.appendChild(li);",
    "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <button id=\"add\">Add</button>\n  <ul id=\"list\"></ul>\n  <script>\n    var count = 0;\n    document.getElementById(\"add\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n      count++;\n      var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      li.textContent = \"Item \" + count;\n      document.getElementById(\"list\").appendChild(li);\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
  ],
  "socratic": [
    "Does createElement put anything on the page by itself?",
    "Which call puts it on the page?",
    "Why use count++ here?"
  ],
  "explain": "In one sentence: what did you learn from “Create Elements”?",
